Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.25,0:00:03.30,Default,s01,0,0,0,,August again, my son.\NThe Dambi Doolloo rain still
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.30,0:00:05.35,Default,s01,0,0,0,,taps this roof,\Nthe way it did when
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.35,0:00:06.35,Default,s01,0,0,0,,you were small.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.23,0:00:10.98,Default,s02,0,0,0,,Eebbisaa, your guitar still\Nleans by the wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.98,0:00:13.48,Default,s02,0,0,0,,You would sit there\Nhumming over your tea,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.48,0:00:15.67,Default,s02,0,0,0,,making fighting songs\Non six strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.25,0:00:18.81,Default,s03,0,0,0,,You weren't just a singer.\NYou taught neighborhood
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.81,0:00:20.37,Default,s03,0,0,0,,kids Qubee—\Nour Oromo alphabet—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.37,0:00:22.62,Default,s03,0,0,0,,so they could finally spell\Ntheir own names.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.24,0:00:26.14,Default,s04,0,0,0,,People listened to your\Ncassettes in secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.14,0:00:29.39,Default,s04,0,0,0,,I still keep your old tape\Nand notebook of lyrics
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.39,0:00:30.67,Default,s04,0,0,0,,folded in my shawl.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.24,0:00:33.56,Default,s05,0,0,0,,Your blue ink still\Nfills this notebook.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.56,0:00:35.22,Default,s05,0,0,0,,Before leaving for\NFinfinnee,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.22,0:00:37.66,Default,s05,0,0,0,,the capital, you sang to me:\N'Mother of a hero,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.66,0:00:38.66,Default,s05,0,0,0,,do not cry.'
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.25,0:00:41.67,Default,s06,0,0,0,,In August 1996,\Na bullet in Finfinnee
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.67,0:00:44.22,Default,s06,0,0,0,,took your voice.\NEver since that night,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.22,0:00:46.57,Default,s06,0,0,0,,this house has been\Nempty and quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.25,0:00:49.76,Default,s07,0,0,0,,For years I couldn't bear\Nto touch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.76,0:00:52.89,Default,s07,0,0,0,,Tonight, the quiet\Nis too heavy. I'm no singer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.89,0:00:54.65,Default,s07,0,0,0,,my son—let me\Ntry one note.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.25,0:00:58.70,Default,s08,0,0,0,,Just one old string...\NThey killed the singer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.70,0:01:00.61,Default,s08,0,0,0,,Eebbisaa. Never the song.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.25,0:01:04.10,Default,s09,0,0,0,,Listen, my son.\NOutside my door,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.10,0:01:07.09,Default,s09,0,0,0,,children who weren't even\Nborn back then still know
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.09,0:01:08.29,Default,s09,0,0,0,,every line you sang.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.25,0:01:12.92,Default,s10,0,0,0,,Hear them? Through the\NDambi Doolloo rain,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.92,0:01:15.86,Default,s10,0,0,0,,they are singing your\Nsongs right back to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.86,0:01:18.01,Default,s10,0,0,0,,Tonight, my son...\NI will not cry.
